  "statementDeltas": [
    {
      "id": "lem-hardy-calderon-zygmund-level-decomposition-produces-atoms",
      "oldHypothesis": "Admissible grand-maximal order N >= N_0(n,p,varphi).",
      "newHypothesis": "Admissible grand-maximal order N >= max{N_0(n,p,varphi), n, floor(n/p)+1}.",
      "exactCurrentStatement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $n\\ge1$, $0<p\\le1$, and let\n$f\\in H^p(\\mathbb R^n)$ with the space and quasi-norm of\n[[def-real-hardy-space-by-a-radial-maximal-function]]. Put\n$s=\\lfloor n(1/p-1)\\rfloor$, let $K\\ge n/p$ be an integer and let\n$\\varphi,\\psi,\\widetilde\\psi$ be the Calderon reproducing pair of flatness $K$\nfrom [[lem-calderon-reproducing-formula-for-the-hardy-decomposition]]. Fix an\nadmissible grand-maximal order\n$N\\ge\\max\\{N_0(n,p,\\varphi),\\,n,\\,\\lfloor n/p\\rfloor+1\\}$. For\n$r\\in\\mathbb Z$ put $\\Omega_r=\\{x:M_Nf(x)>2^r\\}$. Then there are a countable\nfamily $(a_B)$ of $(p,\\infty,s)$-atoms and positive coefficients $\\lambda_B$\nsuch that\n\n1. $\\sum_B\\lambda_B^p\\le C\\|f\\|_{H^p}^p$ with\n   $C=C(n,p,N,K,\\varphi)<\\infty$;\n2. $f=\\sum_B\\lambda_Ba_B$ with convergence in $\\mathcal S'(\\mathbb R^n)$;\n3. each atom $a_B$ is supported in a fixed dilation $B^\\star=7B$ of a ball $B=B(\\xi,\\rho(\\xi)/2)$ of the Whitney-type ball cover of $\\Omega_r$ for the corresponding level $r$, with $\\|a_B\\|_{L^\\infty}\\le|B^\\star|^{-1/p}$ and vanishing moments through order $s$, and the balls $B$ cover $\\Omega_r$ with multiplicity at most $K(n)=785^n$;\n4. the centres and radii are those of [[lem-whitney-type-ball-cover-of-a-proper-open-set]] applied to each nonempty $\\Omega_r$.",
      "reason": "The Facts and proof already required this lower bound. For s=floor(n(1/p-1)), n+s+1=floor(n/p)+1>=n, so the atomic-characterisation consumer already assumes an exactly equivalent order bound. The full H^p and atomic conclusions are unchanged."
    }
  ],
